<section class="wrap service-intro"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Cookies</span></div><p class="eyebrow">COOKIES &amp; SIMILAR TECHNOLOGIES</p><h1>Cookie Policy</h1></section>
<article class="wrap legal-content"><div class="policy-status"><strong>No optional tracking is configured</strong><p>The current production application does not set cookies or use local storage, session storage, advertising pixels or analytics. There are no optional cookie categories to accept or reject in this version.</p></div>
<h2>What are cookies?</h2><p>Cookies are small pieces of information a website can store in your browser. Similar technologies can store or access device information in other ways. Their purposes can include remembering preferences, providing essential functionality or measuring activity.</p>
<h2>What the current website uses</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Cookie information table; scroll horizontally on small screens"><table class="cookie-table"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Current behaviour</th><th>Application storage duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Analytics and advertising</td><td>Not installed or requested by this application</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Preference and session cookies</td><td>No cookies set by application code</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Local and session storage</td><td>Not used by application code</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Enquiry brief</td><td>Created in browser memory; downloadable or passed to your email app for you to review and send</td><td>No persistent application storage; you control the downloaded file</td></tr><tr><td>Maps and external guidance</td><td>Ordinary external links; no embedded map or tracking content</td><td>None set by this application</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Why there is no consent pop-up</h2><p>This version does not use optional cookies or tracking technologies, so it does not ask for consent to features it does not have. You can browse and use the enquiry brief without making a cookie choice. Browser caching, autofill and downloaded files are managed by your browser or device and are separate from application cookie preferences.</p>
<h2>External websites</h2><p>When you follow a map or guidance link, the destination website may use its own cookies or technologies. Its own notice and controls apply. Those services are not loaded simply by viewing this website.</p>
<h2>Before public hosting or additional features</h2><p>The intended production domain is rdbbuildingservices.co.uk and the chosen host is Vercel. The actual hosted domain must be checked before launch, including any enabled CDN, security and traffic-analysis features. Hosting services can process server logs without using browser cookies; any cookies or similar technologies they introduce must be assessed and disclosed with their actual names, providers, purposes and durations.</p><p>If features requiring consent are introduced, they must remain inactive until a valid choice is made. Visitors must be able to reject optional use and change their choice easily. This policy and the actual controls must be updated together; adding this page alone does not establish compliance for a changed site.</p>
<h2>Your browser controls</h2><p>Your browser settings let you inspect and delete cookies and site data. The steps depend on the browser you use. Because this version stores no application cookie preferences, there is no saved consent record or preference to reset here.</p>
<h2>Questions</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk">info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk</a> with cookie questions. Read the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details of the intended hosting arrangement and the remaining pre-launch checks. You can also read the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/direct-marketing-and-privacy-and-electronic-communications/guide-to-pecr/cookies-and-similar-technologies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ICO’s guidance on cookies and similar technologies</a>.</p>
</article></Page>
